<title>USA: St Louis feeder cattle market up $3-$6 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Louis feeder cattle market up $3-$6 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>EAST ST LOUIS, Ill. 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>SPECIAL FEEDER CATTLEAUCTION:   600 head. Compared with last week, feeder</p>
<p>steers under 600 lbs. $3.00-$4.00 per cwt higher, over 600 lbs. steady to $1.00 higher. Feeder heifers $4.00-$6.00 higher. Overall quality comparable to last week's level. Large buyer attendance.</p>
<p>FEEDER STEERS: Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>600-700 lbs. 65.00-70.00, Crossbreds 70.00-72.00</p>
<p>700-800 lbs. 63.00-68.00</p>
<p>Moderately Fleshy:</p>
<p>500-700 lbs. 58.00-66.00</p>
<p>700-900 lbs. 58.00-63.00</p>
<p>Large Frame 2 Holsteins: 800-900 lbs. at 48.00-54.00.</p>
<p>FEEDER HEIFERS: Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>600-700 lbs. 60.00-64.00, Crossbreds 64.00-66.00</p>
<p>700-900 lbs. 57.00-61.00</p>
<p>Moderately Fleshy:</p>
<p>300-700 lbs. 55.00-62.00</p>
<p>Receipts 650   Last week  350   Last Year  350</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
